f the 18th falls on a weekend or a public holiday, the cut-off moves to the last working day before it.\\n\\n## What to submit\\n\\nSubmit one file per team listing every hourly worker with hours and the cost centre the hours are charged to. Blank rows are rejected by the upload page.\\n\\n## Corrections\\n\\nA correction submitted before the cut-off replaces the earlier file entirely. After the cut-off, corrections go to the payroll inbox as a written request and are applied to the following month.\\n\\n## Escalation\\n\\nIf the upload page is unavailable in the hour before the cut-off, email the payroll team and keep the file. Do not send totals in the body of an email.\\n\\n## Paper timesheets\\n\\nTeams without terminal access may send paper timesheets to the payroll office by internal post, to arrive no later than the cut-off.\",\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"slot\": \"title\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Payroll Submission Deadlines (2026 Schedule)\",\n          \"document\": \"source_a.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Payroll Submission Deadlines (2025 Schedule)\",\n          \"document\": \"source_b.md\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"chosen\": \"Payroll Submission Deadlines (2026 Schedule)\",\n      \"reason\": \"Base document's title is current (2026) versus historical (2025).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a6\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Totals must be submitted by 12:00 on the 18th of the month. The 18th is a hard cut-off, not a target, and submissions that arrive after it are held for the following month's run.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Combined a6-a8 for flow and readability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Totals must be submitted by 12:00 on the 18th of the month. The 18th is a hard cut-off, not a target, and submissions that arrive after it are held 